    },
    "body": "Reverse facts with unfamiliar lowercase values could store only a suffix: `Record: moss dale holds selvi` stored `dale`, so a correct historical read still emitted an incomplete answer. This change refines two existing signed-H4 code rows, making the full admitted phrase win while preserving the dictionary, feature/admission law, exact occurrence endpoints and other model parameters. An outer artifact witness restores the complete parent and supplies a matched removal control.\n\nThe combined model `57cee4c4` is retained after actual generated behavior passed: 36/36 new construction answers (parent 30/36), 53/53 historical targets, all 1,264 inherited construction comparisons, and a separately frozen 216/216 fresh answer/span gate (parent 192/216) with 144/144 exact historical selections and all removal controls matching the parent. Replaying the previous negative draw improves 44/64 to 64/64 complete historical answers.\n\nValidation: 33 focused tests; eight actual historical→current→arithmetic sequences with 1,880 input and 264 output checkpoint positions; 394 native API checks; 14 prior behavior/control reports with zero checked differences; 12 histories; 24-case word/Rust transfer; and 24/24 ordinary plus 24/24 stress for both Copy→Add and action emission. Actual generated Rust compiles and executes. Formatting and claim wording are checked locally. The retained query-owner panel keeps all 72 answers/stops/source decisions and all other state exact while repairing 72 old spans; its raw full-state equality remains 0/72. The opened previous negative panel likewise discloses its 16 intended untargeted span repairs and raw equality count. Original wrapper/comparator failures remain in evidence.\n\nThe canonical state and roadmap now point to version-aware owner/value composition over an explicitly selected historical record. General prose, general reasoning/program synthesis, alpha/frontier capability and complete-path energy remain unqualified. The full suite, new-artifact browser/WASM/HTTP and allocation/energy instrumentation were not run. Required PR/merge-group statuses are compatibility acknowledgements; they are not the local test results above. All previous artifacts and charges are preserved; no unique deletion or paid external compute occurred.\n\nReferences #973\n",
